  "notes": "A career songwriter turned artist, and the model is built around that fact because the entry is: \"hook-first and songwriter-shaped — a short, immediately memorable phrase repeated with variation\". That is `structure` `riff_loop` with `twoBarCellRepeat` on, `endVariation` on and a small `motifPitchCount`, which is the closest this schema gets to \"repeated with variation\". Harmony is richer than the lane norm on the entry's own claim — \"4-chord cycles and real cadences inherited from her songwriting career, plus gospel passing chords and a modulating final chorus\" — so the families cadence and `susOrDimProb` carries the passing chords. The modelled band is the half-time one (128–150 read) with the trap kit the entry puts on the singles; the 90s swung kit on the album material is why `fullTimeVariantProb` is non-trivial and the tambourine sits in the perc lanes. \"Finger-snaps as a constant layer\" is a `snap` lane at a high density. ⚠ `confidence` is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low — \"her songwriter-to-artist route and lane position are sourced; parametric detail is inference\". ⚠ Every drum number, the swing amount, the 808 figures and both melody bands are therefore **INFERRED**. ⚠ `session.bpm.mode` is **INFERRED**: the number is not stated in the entry, and it is an authored centre of gravity inside the band the entry does state. ⚠ **`session.keys` is INFERRED.** The entry's Keys line describes the harmonic grammar but names no key centre, so these values and their weights are an authored choice — no key in this set is stated in the research.",
